WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.000
Why does Azure need a gate of its own?

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.325
Service Health shows service
issues, planned maintenance,

3
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:09.125
health advisories and security
advisories for each subscription.

4
00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:13.584
But the portal tells nobody unless
someone created a Service Health alert,

5
00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:18.475
and an alert fires only for the subscriptions,
services and regions its rule names.

6
00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:21.827
Microsoft's own F A Q gives
a rule that left out the

7
00:00:21.827 --> 00:00:25.850
affected subscription as a
reason an alert never arrived.

8
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.967
Azure Resource Graph answers the same
questions for every subscription in scope with

9
00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:34.165
one query, against its Service
Health resources table,

10
00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:37.150
and Microsoft Learn
publishes the sample queries.

11
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.225
So this module does two things.

12
00:00:39.225 --> 00:00:42.863
It collects with the kit's query,
built from Learn's samples.

13
00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:46.694
And it plans Service Health alerts
at scale with Azure Policy,

14
00:00:46.694 --> 00:00:49.820
as a plan that's applied
only with an approved hash.
